 "answer": "Per member the joint fit reads sh510300 own 0.452 [0.325, 0.578] vs aggregate -0.201 [-0.313, -0.089] (corr 0.930) -> both_channels_live; sh510050 own 0.734 [0.651, 0.818] vs aggregate -0.487 [-0.545, -0.429] (corr 0.910) -> both_channels_live; sh510500 own -0.122 [-0.155, -0.089] vs aggregate 0.302 [0.226, 0.377] (corr 0.749) -> both_channels_live; sh512100 own -0.147 [-0.180, -0.114] vs aggregate 0.638 [0.533, 0.743] (corr 0.871) -> both_channels_live; sh588000 own 0.188 [0.054, 0.322] vs aggregate 0.258 [0.028, 0.488] (corr 0.854) -> unresolved; pooled with member intercepts b_own = 0.029 [0.010, 0.048] and b_agg = 0.039 [0.009, 0.069] at a bar of t=2.87 (median |corr| 0.871), giving unresolved. The aggregate turnover level is 0.9455 autocorrelated, so the lagged-level block E233 carries is only computable on 3 of 5 sleeves and agrees in sign on 0; the spec check therefore reads unavailable. Book-scaling elasticity b_own + b_agg = 0.068. Re-priced, binary_low linear 1538.8 -> one aggregate charge 1538.8 -> five per-sleeve charges 5193.2 bp (split/aggregate 3.375); tilt_step linear 1610.6 -> one aggregate charge 3002.5 -> five per-sleeve charges 9364.3 bp (split/aggregate 3.119); tilt_linear linear 1706.0 -> one aggregate charge 10729.9 -> five per-sleeve charges 29458.0 bp (split/aggregate 2.745). Conclusion: 2 of 5 sleeves price their OWN turnover with a negative elasticity (sh510500, sh512100) -- a move is priced smaller when the sleeve's own turnover is larger, which no impact story produces. The level specification is therefore inadequate: the family's single exponent (0.622) is a mixture of two offsetting channels, and the pooled book-scaling elasticity that survives both (0.068) is an artefact of that cancellation. No figure here is a bill; the question needs a share-and-difference design.",
